**Notes:**
Ptolemy, a Greco-Roman astronomer who lived around 100–170 CE, thought that an enormous far-southern landmass must exist in order to provide a planetary counterweight to the large continents of the north.

150 AD — Ptolemy published *Geographia*, which notes Terra Australis Incognita.

**⚠️ This is the origin of the idea of Antarctica in the Western intellectual tradition — but it is a theoretical inference, not observation.** The reasoning was counterweight symmetry, not exploration. This distinction is critical for your project.

